@status workshop experiment 2026-09-12; NOT assayed; the s4 counterexample is FIXED at source (d0741b04: typed evidence + in-band :s4-evidence); live flip pending JVM reload — until then the live page still shows s4=false, which is now a stale rendering, not an untyped absence.

! conclusion:
  A composed claim (a cascade, a page, a report) may not present itself
  as complete while its honest holes are unrecorded: every composition
  step that could have holes must either carry them or carry a typed
  statement that none were found.

  + context:
    The cascade-live map composes O1xO4=73 missions and reports
    s5-composed=true; the honest-holes dimension is empty, so s4 reads
    false. Empty-or-unread is exactly the ambiguity the two-wire
    discipline exists to kill: an absent hole list is not evidence of no
    holes.

  + IF:
    A composition (overlap, join, cascade, rendered summary) is about to
    be published or scored.

  + HOWEVER:
    Enumerating holes has cost and some dimensions genuinely have none;
    demanding a hole census everywhere would price composition out.
    Scope: the composition's OWN dimensions, not the whole register.

  + THEN:
    Before publish: for each composed dimension, emit either the hole
    list or a typed none {:checked-dimensions [...] :holes-found 0};
    s4 becomes true only on typed evidence. Publishing with s4=false is
    permitted only with the falsity rendered in-band (the page already
    does this — the standard is honest; the substrate is not yet).

  + BECAUSE:
    A composition that hides its holes teaches its readers a map with no
    fog on it — and fogless maps are how three agents believed a dirty
    tree (the README-inbox-zero lesson) and how monitors degrade toward
    "fine" (2026-08-19). Honesty about gaps is a precondition for the
    apex thesis: work steers itself only if it can see where it isn't.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Emit the typed none-or-holes record for O5 and flip s4 honestly.]
    next[Add s4-style gates to the other published compositions (issue board's no-carrying-packet count is the same shape).]
